    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0537" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.51/215a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-05T20:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>455. With the closing of the Paris office of the Embassy Vichy becomes the
                    permanent seat of the American Embassy to France. Beginning July 1 Department
                    contemplates placing Vichy on permanent status and making allotments for
                    operating expenses from the regular appropriations.…</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
